ependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"<!-- Before creating a bug report, try disabling browser extensions to see if the bug is still present. -->\r\n\r\n<!-- If you're having trouble updating your profile, it is likely because you logged in separately with GitHub & Twitter. Please check if this is the case before creating a bug report, and email yo@dev.to so we can merge your accounts. -->\r\n\r\n**Describe the bug**\r\n\r\n<!-- A clear and concise description of what the bug is. -->\r\nSometimes when joining a new room, the room that gets displayed to the user is actually a previously joined room and not the room that the user has just joined. This feels unintuitive and might lead to confusion.\r\n\r\n**To Reproduce**\r\n\r\n<!-- Steps to reproduce the behavior: -->\r\n\r\n<!-- 1. Go to '...' -->\r\n<!-- 2. Click on '....' -->\r\n<!-- 3. Scroll down to '....' -->\r\n<!-- 4. See error -->\r\n\r\n**Expected behavior**\r\n\r\n<!-- A clear and concise description of what you expected to happen. -->\r\nUpon joining a new room, the user should always be taken to that room.\r\n\r\n**Screenshots**\r\n\r\n<!-- If applicable, add screenshots to help explain your problem. -->\r\n![dev_connect_wrong-room-after-accepting-invite](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/27379918/88437571-59b0c180-cdcc-11ea-9e45-9709bcaadf69.gif)\r\nHere you can see the room the user wants to join is called \"show-and-tell\", but upon accepting the invite, the room that displays is one that the user previously joined, called \"watercooler\".\r\n\r\n**Desktop (please complete the following information):**\r\n\r\n- OS: Mac\r\n- Browser: Chrome\r\n- Version: 83.0.4103.116\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"benhalpern","id":3102842,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMDI4NDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3102842?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benhalpern","html_url":"https://github.com/benhalpern","followers_